                <pb facs="0204" n="198" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg198"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Sir Julian Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In reply to your excellency’s note
                    of the 10th instant inclosing a memorandum of certain arrangements agreed upon
                    between our respective Governments for giving effect during the year 1891 to the
                    fur-seal fishery regulations prescribed by the award of the Bering Sea tribunal
                    of Arbitration, I have the honor to state that I approve of the memorandum as
                    containing a correct record of the arrangements agreed upon.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
